{"id":"a6801ecc09e4f5fd","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-global-choice.md","title":"Global Choice","display":"thm-global-choice — Global Choice","type":"axiom","metadata":{"type":"axiom","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-global-choice","aliases":["58-thm-global-choice"],"display":"thm-global-choice — Global Choice","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-class.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"axiom"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-global-choice"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-global-choice</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-global-choice — Global Choice"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" href=\"?note=ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-class.md\">../batch11/58-df-class.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> is a metatheoretic class relation and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\">\\(\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\)</span> is the class quantifier.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)\\)</span> is defined here by a functional graph condition; it is not a set predicate on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice\\text{-}function}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall x\\in V\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\}\\;\n\\exists!y\\in x\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice\\text{-}function}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall x\\in V\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\}\\;\n\\exists!y\\in x\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}F\\;\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}F\\;\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The chooser is a proper-class graph, so this is naturally a class-theory axiom rather than a set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\in V\">\\(F\\in V\\)</span>; functionality and choice are both expanded in the displayed definition.</li>\n<li>Global choice implies ordinary set choice but is stronger as a class assertion.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-class.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca2a9c9166fa8cce","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-class.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice\\text{-}function}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall x\\in V\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\}\\;\n\\exists!y\\in x\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}global\\text{-}choice}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\vdash\n\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}F\\;\n\\mathrm{GlobalChoiceFunction}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(F).","display":true},{"tex":"F\\in V","display":false}],"bytes":1169,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4185","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-thm-global-choice.md|58-thm-global-choice]]（batch10）"}],"outgoing":["ca2a9c9166fa8cce"]}